#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175619 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "2f4571af-99cf-5a4a-9998-fb6a0f7d6be9" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-11004" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\tan x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n1. The zeros of the function are at $x = \\pi n$.\n2. The function has asymptotes at $x = 2\\pi n$.\n3. The range of the function is $y\\in [-1,1]$." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\tan x$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3558/Source/Images/8b2ecc027eb04e0cb4a12ecd0b0191cf.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The zeros occur at $x=0, \\pm \\pi, \\pm2\\pi,\\ldots$, which can be written as $x=n\\pi$.\n- Statement II is false. The function has an asymptote at $x = \\dfrac \\pi 2$ and the period is $\\pi$. Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x = \\dfrac \\pi 2 + \\pi n$.\n- Statement III is false. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $y\\in (-\\infty, \\infty)$.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175620 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eed0c7c3-0bb5-56eb-a9ca-9ec4dc7b3efe" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Tangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "f4649856-d777-5468-a7f4-df50479e36d7" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-11005" :question/problem "If $\\tan\\left(x\\right) = -2$ for some value of $x$, then find the value of $\\tan\\left(x-2\\pi\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\tan x$ is $\\pi$. Therefore, for any integer $n$, we have\n\n$$\n\\tan x = \\tan (x+n\\pi)\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\tan x &= \\tan (x + (-2) \\cdot π) = \\tan (x - 2π)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\tan\\left(x\\right) = -2\n$$\n\nwe get that\n\n$$\n\\tan\\left(x-2\\pi\\right) = -2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175628 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66a1733a-d7bb-5c86-a154-9e54422053a7" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Oddness Property of the Tangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "0b146642-914c-52ce-9939-86752e95dcd2" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-11013" :question/problem "If $\\tan x = -\\dfrac{2}{3}$, find the value of $\\tan (-x+7\\pi)$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=\\tan{x}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3558/Source/Images/d01abb298d92d64b71126490ab06b4ed.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $\\tan{x}$ is $\\pi$.\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $\\tan{x}$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n$\\tan(-x) = -\\tan{x}$.\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $\\tan{x}$, we have\n$\\tan (-x + 7π)|= \\tan (-x + π \\cdot 7); = \\tan (-x)$.\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $\\tan{x}$, we have\n$\\tan (-x)|=-\\tan x; = - (-\\frac{2}{3})$.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\tan (-x+7\\pi)=\\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176269 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66a1733a-d7bb-5c86-a154-9e54422053a7" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Oddness Property of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3a94382-6334-5d6e-b5ba-42e4999251d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174277} {:answer/id #uuid "cafcc4e9-a02b-55d7-aaaa-ed8952cc5efb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174278} {:answer/id #uuid "cdaaa308-e9e5-5c23-a80b-cffbaa339154" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174279} {:answer/id #uuid "5894476c-02e6-5f0b-adf2-f1af972e7a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174280} {:answer/id #uuid "6018e45d-a275-5ed6-b668-e5ef2a26402b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3a94382-6334-5d6e-b5ba-42e4999251d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174277} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d9c5fac-2ff8-5b25-91eb-1cc1a80648d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174276}] :question/id #uuid "ccd7ae50-1c4e-5bcc-8b8b-d405f5154f0b" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-136548" :question/problem "If $\\tan a =-2$, then $\\tan (-a) =$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176376 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85f53242-b161-5061-b2e6-21454c0aa47a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174801} {:answer/id #uuid "dc875309-87cf-5386-8c20-9cac6e4c3c23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174802} {:answer/id #uuid "ee521ecc-bde5-51e0-a9c7-9fa0450ac9b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174803} {:answer/id #uuid "4505287a-b44e-5953-bdfd-6fc4749e3020" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174804} {:answer/id #uuid "647bb7e7-374a-5350-8015-2a7421e5c3a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4505287a-b44e-5953-bdfd-6fc4749e3020" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174804} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ee3205f-bac2-5d75-a8b4-6c10b6d8d2e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174800}] :question/id #uuid "ac898e3a-bbc1-536e-8415-2d3fbc798e28" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-27638" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\tan x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n1. The function has asymptotes at $x = nπ$.\n2. The function returns only positive values on the intervals $(πn, \\frac{π}{2} + πn)$.\n3. The function has zeros at $x = \\frac{π}{2} + nπ$."}]}
